    faqs: [['How is GEO different from AEO?', 'AEO concentrates on clear answers to specific questions. GEO also examines the broader picture of your brand, its topics and supporting sources. A practical programme may include both.'], ['Is a citation the same as a link?', 'A platform may mention a name, show a source citation or provide a clickable referral. Those are different observations and should be reported separately.'], ['Do all AI platforms behave alike?', 'No. Their source selection and presentation differ, and available access guidance can change. Research should name the platforms being reviewed.'], ['Can GEO enquiries be attributed?', 'Some referrals are visible in analytics, while others are not. Customer-reported discovery can supplement the evidence but should not be presented as precise platform attribution.'], ['What can JustGrow control?', 'We can improve agreed content and information consistency, document research and conduct approved outreach. We cannot control generated answers or independent editorial decisions.']],
