    problem: 'Visitors should not have to interpret a vague heading or search across several pages to understand your offer. Repeated titles, thin explanations and weak internal links make pages harder to distinguish. More keywords will not solve a mismatch between a visitor’s question and the page’s purpose.',
    definition: 'On-page SEO improves the content and structure of individual URLs. It combines search-intent alignment with readable information and a useful next step. It works alongside technical SEO, which looks at wider crawl, indexation and site infrastructure issues.',
