    definition: 'Off-page SEO concerns relevant signals and discovery beyond your own website. It can include backlink review, link reclamation, appropriate listings and earned editorial mentions. The starting question is whether a reference would make sense to a real reader, rather than whether a tool assigns the domain a high score.',
    scope: [["Backlink profile audit","Review existing referring sites, relevant mentions and lost links. We assess context and patterns to identify useful opportunities and concerns that need closer investigation."],["Competitor link research","Explore where relevant competitors earn coverage and why. We use those findings to discover publications and resource gaps that fit your business."],["Editorial outreach","Approach suitable publishers with approved expertise, guides or resources that help their readers. Each pitch connects a useful contribution to a relevant destination page."],["Link reclamation","Identify lost references, broken destination links and unlinked brand mentions. Where appropriate, we ask the site owner to restore or add an accurate reference."],["Business citations and listings","Review industry and local directories that real customers use. We prioritise accurate information and relevant listings, with local profile work agreed separately when needed."],["Coverage and referral reporting","Document outreach, responses, live placements and mentions. Review referral visits and attributable enquiries where tracking allows, then refine the next priorities."]],
    deliverables: ['Backlink and mention review', 'Relevant opportunity shortlist', 'Approved outreach plan and activity log', 'Earned placement and mention report'],
    process: [['Review', 'Understand existing references and useful assets.'], ['Select', 'Choose opportunities with an identifiable reader benefit.'], ['Approach', 'Use approved, individual outreach and accurate claims.'], ['Assess', 'Record outcomes, relevant referrals and follow-up opportunities.']],
    inputs: 'Approved business facts, useful resources, a contact identity you authorise and clarity on who approves outreach. Any prior coverage or relationships help avoid duplicate approaches and inappropriate claims.',
    measures: "We report relevant referring sites, earned mentions, restored links and referral traffic, alongside attributable enquiries where tracking is available. Third-party authority scores can add context, but lead quality and useful coverage matter more than a headline link count.",
